KT COURIERS PRIVACY POLICY
Effective Date: 9 August 2026
Last Updated: 9 August 2026
KT COURIERS ("KT Couriers", "we", "us", "our") is committed to protecting the privacy and personal information of our customers, vendors, delivery personnel, business partners, website visitors and other users of our services.
This Privacy Policy explains how KT Couriers collects, uses, stores, protects and shares personal information when you access or use our website, mobile applications, marketplace, delivery services, vendor services, customer services and other related services (collectively referred to as the "Services").
KT Couriers operates in accordance with applicable South African privacy and data-protection legislation, including the Protection of Personal Information Act 4 of 2013 (POPIA), where applicable.
By using our Services, creating an account, placing an order, registering as a vendor or delivery partner, or otherwise providing personal information to KT Couriers, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.
1. WHO WE ARE
KT Couriers is a marketplace and logistics platform that connects customers with businesses, vendors and delivery personnel.
Our Services may include:
Online marketplace services;
Food and grocery deliveries;
Pharmacy and store deliveries;
E-commerce orders;
Parcel deliveries;
Business collections and deliveries;
Same-day and scheduled deliveries;
Business-to-business delivery services;
Vendor and merchant services;
Customer support;
Delivery tracking and related logistics services.
For purposes of POPIA, KT Couriers may act as a responsible party in relation to personal information that we process for our own business and platform purposes.
Where third-party vendors or service providers independently process information for their own purposes, they may have their own privacy obligations and policies.
2. INFORMATION WE COLLECT
Depending on how you use our Services, we may collect the following categories of personal information.
2.1 Customer Information
This may include:
Full name;
Email address;
Mobile or telephone number;
Billing information;
Delivery address;
Collection address;
Account information;
Order history;
Customer preferences;
Communication records;
Information provided when contacting customer support.
2.2 Vendor Information
If you register or operate a business on the KT Couriers marketplace, we may collect:
Owner or authorised representative's name;
Business name;
Business contact details;
Business address;
Email address;
Telephone number;
Banking or payment information where required;
Business registration information;
Tax or VAT information where applicable;
Product and service information;
Store information;
Documents required for verification;
Communications relating to the vendor account.
2.3 Delivery Personnel Information
If you apply to or operate as a delivery partner, driver or courier, we may collect information necessary to onboard and manage the delivery relationship, including:
Full name;
Contact details;
Identification information;
Address;
Driver's licence information;
Vehicle information;
Banking or payment information;
Delivery activity;
Location information;
Verification information;
Documents required for onboarding;
Information relating to safety, compliance and account management.
Where legally permitted and necessary for on boarding or security purposes, additional verification information may be collected.
2.4 Order and Transaction Information
When you place or fulfil an order, we may collect:
Products or services ordered;
Vendor selected;
Order number;
Collection and delivery details;
Delivery instructions;
Transaction date and time;
Order value;
Delivery fee;
Payment status;
Refund information;
Transaction history.
2.5 Location Information
KT Couriers may process location information where necessary to provide delivery and marketplace functionality.
This may include:
Delivery location;
Collection location;
Approximate device location;
Driver location while performing a delivery;
Route and delivery-tracking information.
Location information may be used to calculate delivery distances, identify delivery zones, assist with dispatching, provide delivery tracking and improve logistics operations.
Where location access is optional for a particular Service, you may manage location permissions through your device settings. Certain Services may not function correctly without the location information required to perform them.
2.6 Device and Technical Information
When you access our website or applications, we may automatically collect certain technical information, including:
IP address;
Browser type;
Operating system;
Device type;
Device identifiers;
Application information;
Login information;
Date and time of access;
Referring website;
Technical and diagnostic information.
2.7 Usage Information
We may collect information about how you interact with our Services, including:
Pages visited;
Features used;
Searches;
Products viewed;
Orders placed;
Clicks and interactions;
App activity;
Preferences;
Error reports and diagnostic information.
3. HOW WE COLLECT INFORMATION
We may collect personal information:
Directly from you;
When you create an account;
When you place or fulfil an order;
When you register a business;
When you apply as a delivery partner;
When you contact customer support;
Through our website or mobile applications;
Through cookies and similar technologies;
From payment and transaction service providers;
From delivery and technology service providers;
From publicly available sources where lawful;
From other parties where permitted by law.
We will seek to collect only information that is reasonably necessary for a specific and legitimate purpose.
4. HOW WE USE PERSONAL INFORMATION
We may use personal information for the following purposes:
4.1 Providing Our Services
To:
Create and manage accounts;
Process orders;
Connect customers with vendors;
Assign and manage deliveries;
Process collections;
Calculate delivery fees;
Track deliveries;
Provide customer support;
Process refunds and cancellations;
Manage vendor accounts;
Manage delivery-partner accounts.
4.2 Payments and Transactions
We may process information necessary to facilitate payments, refunds, settlements and other financial transactions through our payment service providers.
KT Couriers may not directly store complete payment-card information where payment processing is handled by a third-party payment provider.
Payment providers may process information in accordance with their own privacy policies.
4.3 Platform Improvement
We may use information to:
Improve our marketplace;
Improve delivery operations;
Analyse platform performance;
Understand customer behaviour;
Improve user experience;
Develop new features;
Identify technical problems;
Monitor platform performance.
4.4 Communication
We may use your information to communicate with you regarding:
Orders;
Deliveries;
Account activity;
Payments;
Refunds;
Service updates;
Security matters;
Customer support;
Important notices;
Changes to our Services.
4.5 Marketing
Subject to applicable law and your marketing preferences, KT Couriers may use your contact information to provide information about:
Promotions;
Special offers;
New services;
Vendors;
Marketplace campaigns;
Delivery offers;
Business opportunities;
KT Couriers initiatives.
Where POPIA requires consent for unsolicited electronic direct marketing, we will obtain and manage such consent as required by law. The South African Information Regulator confirms that POPIA regulates unsolicited electronic direct marketing such as email, SMS, telephone and push notifications.
You may opt out of marketing communications at any time by using the unsubscribe mechanism provided, changing your communication preferences, or contacting us.
4.6 Fraud and Security
We may process information to:
Prevent fraud;
Detect suspicious activity;
Protect customers, vendors and delivery personnel;
Protect our platform;
Investigate misuse;
Enforce our Terms and Conditions;
Protect our rights and property.
4.7 Legal and Regulatory Compliance
We may process and disclose information where reasonably necessary to:
Comply with applicable laws;
Respond to lawful requests;
Comply with court orders;
Cooperate with law-enforcement authorities;
Meet regulatory requirements;
Establish, exercise or defend legal claims.
5. SHARING OF PERSONAL INFORMATION
KT Couriers does not sell personal information as a business practice.
We may share relevant personal information with third parties where necessary to provide our Services, operate our business, comply with legal requirements or otherwise process information lawfully.
These parties may include:
5.1 Vendors and Marketplace Businesses
Where necessary to fulfil an order, we may provide a vendor with relevant customer information, such as:
Customer name;
Order details;
Collection or delivery information;
Contact information where necessary;
Delivery instructions.
5.2 Delivery Personnel
Where necessary to complete a delivery, delivery personnel may receive information such as:
Customer name;
Collection address;
Delivery address;
Contact number;
Order information;
Delivery instructions.
Delivery personnel may only use such information for legitimate delivery and service purposes.
5.3 Technology and Service Providers
We may use third-party providers for services such as:
Hosting;
Cloud storage;
Payment processing;
Mapping and location services;
SMS and communication services;
Email services;
Analytics;
Customer support;
Fraud prevention;
Identity or business verification;
Software and technical infrastructure.
These providers may process personal information on our behalf and may be required to implement appropriate safeguards.
5.4 Business Partners
Where appropriate and lawful, information may be shared with business partners to support services, partnerships, promotions or other legitimate business activities.
Where consent is legally required, KT Couriers will obtain the appropriate consent before sharing personal information for that purpose.
5.5 Legal and Regulatory Authorities
We may disclose information to government authorities, law enforcement, regulators, courts or other authorised parties where required or permitted by law.
5.6 Business Transfers
If KT Couriers undergoes a merger, acquisition, restructuring, investment, sale of assets or similar transaction, personal information may form part of the transferred business assets, subject to applicable privacy laws.
6. LOCATION AND DELIVERY TRACKING
Location information is an important part of our delivery platform.
We may use location information to:
Identify collection and delivery locations;
Calculate delivery distances;
Calculate delivery pricing;
Allocate delivery jobs;
Monitor delivery progress;
Provide estimated arrival information;
Improve routing;
Confirm delivery;
Protect the security of deliveries;
Investigate delivery disputes.
Delivery personnel may be required to enable location services while actively performing deliveries.
KT Couriers will not use location information for purposes unrelated to legitimate platform, delivery, safety, security or operational requirements unless permitted by law or otherwise authorised.
7. COOKIES AND TRACKING TECHNOLOGIES
KT Couriers may use cookies, pixels, SDKs, analytics tools and similar technologies.
These technologies may help us:
Keep users logged in;
Remember preferences;
Improve website and application performance;
Understand how our Services are used;
Analyse traffic;
Detect technical issues;
Improve advertising and marketing;
Measure campaign performance;
Improve security.
You may be able to control cookies through your browser or device settings.
Disabling certain cookies may affect the functionality of some Services.
Where required by law, KT Couriers will provide appropriate notice and obtain consent for non-essential cookies or similar technologies.
8. THIRD-PARTY SERVICES AND LINKS
Our Services may contain links, integrations or connections to third-party websites, applications, payment providers, mapping services, social-media platforms or other services.
KT Couriers is not responsible for the privacy practices of third parties that operate independently from us.
We encourage users to review the privacy policies of third-party services before providing personal information to them.
9. DATA SECURITY
KT Couriers takes reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal information against:
Unauthorised access;
Unauthorised disclosure;
Loss;
Misuse;
Alteration;
Destruction;
Accidental disclosure.
Security measures may include access controls, authentication, secure systems, monitoring, restricted access and other safeguards appropriate to the nature of the information and the risks involved.
However, no electronic transmission or storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
If KT Couriers becomes aware of a security compromise involving personal information, we will take appropriate steps in accordance with applicable law.
10. HOW LONG WE KEEP INFORMATION
We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes for which it was collected, including:
Providing Services;
Maintaining business and transaction records;
Resolving disputes;
Preventing fraud;
Meeting legal and regulatory obligations;
Enforcing agreements;
Protecting our legal rights.
Different categories of information may be retained for different periods.
When personal information is no longer required, we will take reasonable steps to securely delete, destroy, anonymise or otherwise dispose of it, subject to applicable legal and operational requirements.
11. YOUR PRIVACY RIGHTS
Subject to applicable law, you may have the right to:
Access
Request confirmation of whether KT Couriers holds personal information about you and request access to such information.
Correction
Request that inaccurate, incomplete or outdated information be corrected or updated.
Deletion
Request deletion or removal of personal information where legally permitted.
Objection
Object to certain forms of processing of your personal information where permitted by law.
Direct Marketing
Object to or withdraw consent for direct marketing communications in accordance with applicable law.
Withdrawal of Consent
Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw that consent, subject to any legal consequences or other lawful basis for continued processing.
Data Portability
Where applicable and reasonably possible, request your information in a usable format.
Complaint
You may contact KT Couriers regarding concerns about our processing of your personal information.
The Information Regulator of South Africa also provides mechanisms for POPIA complaints and security-compromise reporting.
12. HOW TO EXERCISE YOUR RIGHTS
To request access, correction, deletion, objection or other privacy-related assistance, contact:
Email: support@ktcouriers.com
Please provide enough information for us to identify your account and understand your request.
We may need to verify your identity before processing certain requests in order to protect your personal information from unauthorised disclosure.
We will respond to legitimate requests within the period required by applicable law.
13. CHILDREN'S PRIVACY
Our Services are not intended for children under the age of 18 unless otherwise expressly permitted by applicable law and appropriate consent has been obtained.
We do not knowingly collect personal information from children in circumstances where such collection is prohibited by law.
If you believe that a child has provided personal information to KT Couriers unlawfully, please contact us at: support@ktcouriers.com
14. INTERNATIONAL DATA TRANSFERS
Some of our technology, hosting, payment, communication, mapping, analytics or other service providers may operate outside South Africa.
As a result, personal information may be processed or stored outside South Africa where permitted by applicable law.
Where personal information is transferred across borders, KT Couriers will take reasonable steps to ensure that the transfer complies with applicable legal requirements and that appropriate protections are in place.
POPIA contains specific requirements relating to transborder flows of personal information, and certain transfers may require additional safeguards or authorisation depending on the circumstances.
15. ACCURACY OF PERSONAL INFORMATION
We aim to maintain accurate and reasonably up-to-date personal information.
You are responsible for ensuring that information provided to KT Couriers is accurate, complete and current.
If your information changes, you should update your account where this functionality is available or contact us.
16. YOUR RESPONSIBILITIES
You should take reasonable steps to protect your own personal information, including:
Keeping your account password confidential;
Not sharing account credentials;
Using appropriate device security;
Logging out of shared devices;
Reporting suspicious account activity;
Providing accurate information;
Not submitting another person's personal information without lawful authority.
17. VENDOR AND DELIVERY PARTNER PRIVACY
Vendors and delivery personnel may receive personal information belonging to customers as part of fulfilling orders or providing Services.
Such information must only be used for legitimate purposes connected to the order or Service.
Vendors and delivery personnel must not:
Sell customer information;
Use customer information for unrelated marketing without lawful authority;
Share customer information unnecessarily;
Store customer information longer than reasonably necessary;
Use customer information for personal purposes;
Disclose customer information to unauthorised persons.
A breach of these requirements may result in suspension or termination of access to KT Couriers Services and may also result in legal action where appropriate.
18. MARKETING AND COMMUNICATION PREFERENCES
KT Couriers may communicate with you through channels such as:
Email;
Whatsapp
SMS;
Telephone;
Push notifications;
WhatsApp or similar communication channels where applicable;
In-platform notifications.
Transactional and service-related communications may still be sent even where you have opted out of promotional marketing, where the communication is necessary to provide the Services or fulfil a legal or contractual obligation.
Marketing communications will be handled in accordance with applicable law.
19. DATA BREACHES AND SECURITY INCIDENTS
If KT Couriers experiences a security compromise involving personal information, we will assess the incident and take appropriate steps as required by applicable law.
